===Alternative forms===
* [[tzetze]], [[tsetze]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|tn|en}} {{term|tsetse|lang=tn}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|tsetse}}

# Any [[fly]] of the [[genus]] {{taxlink|Glossina|genus}}, native to [[Africa]], that feeds on human and animal blood; known primarily as a carrier of parasitic [[trypanosome]]s.

====Usage notes====
* Particularly in North American English, this insect is most commonly referred to as a "tsetse fly."

